  "title": "wslua: Catch more types of exceptions",
  "description": "We have to do various cleanup after calling a Lua dissector, so\ncatch more types of dissector errors in the Lua handling instead\nof letting, e.g., BoundsError (ran off packet captured length,\nand captured length < reported length, so packet was truncated\nduring capture.) bubble up to packet-frame.c\n\nPossibly not all of these error types need the Lua error and\nLua traceback in the tree, but they do need to be caught here.\n\nFix #18681.",
